                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-10T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                                1927—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>187. Your 318, November 4, 3 p.m. Department’s 173, October 29, 1 p.m. was sent
                    on recommendation of Minister for Foreign Affairs contained in your 289, October
                    24, 3 p.m. concurred in by you. In view of change in situation Department has no
                    objection to procedure agreed to by both parties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
